  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "ML-C101-kuriya",
      "sequence": 3620,
      "title": "കുറിയ (kuṟiya) — short, of a person",
      "headword": "കുറിയ",
      "romanization": "kuṟiya",
      "gloss": "short — built exactly like ചെറിയ, and not a second word for it",
      "script": "malayalam",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:b3bb57a09e1505c1",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Say small. Then say he."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "കുറിയ — kuṟiya — short, said of a person's height."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "അവൻ കുറിയ കുട്ടിയാണ്. — avan kuṟiya kuṭṭiyāṇŭ — \"He is a short child.\""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Put it beside the word you already have and the shape is the same."
            },
            {
              "kind": "table",
              "headers": [
                "word",
                "romanized"
              ],
              "columns": 2,
              "rowCount": 2,
              "utterances": [
                "word: ചെറിയ. romanized: ceṟiya.",
                "word: കുറിയ. romanized: kuṟiya."
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Same റ, same -ിയ ending, same job in the sentence: in front of the noun, unchanged, exactly as the adjective chapter said."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What differs is the meaning, not the shape. ചെറിയ is small — little, not much of it. കുറിയ (kuṟiya) is short — not long, and of a person, not tall. A child can be ചെറിയ and a child can be കുറിയ (kuṟiya), and those say two different things about the child."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "kuṟiya",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *kuṟiya*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "ceṟiya, then kuṟiya, and hear how little separates them",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *ceṟiya*, then *kuṟiya*, and hear how little separates them]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "avan kuṟiya kuṭṭiyāṇŭ",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *avan kuṟiya kuṭṭiyāṇŭ*]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What is short, of a person? (കുറിയ (kuṟiya).) Which word you already had is built the same way? (ചെറിയ.) And where does it stand? (In front of the noun, unchanged.)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ML-C101-melinja",
      "sequence": 3630,
      "title": "മെലിഞ്ഞ (meliñña) — thin",
      "headword": "മെലിഞ്ഞ",
      "romanization": "meliñña",
      "gloss": "thin, of a person — an adjective that ends in -a without ending in -iya",
      "script": "malayalam",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:3a85d16f1f95b48c",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Say short, of a person. Where does it stand?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "മെലിഞ്ഞ — meliñña — thin, said of a person's build."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "മെലിഞ്ഞ കുട്ടി — meliñña kuṭṭi — \"a thin child.\""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The ending is the constant; the shape in front of it never was."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "വലിയ, നല്ല, പുതിയ, പഴയ, ചെറിയ, and now കുറിയ (kuṟiya) — every adjective the book has put in front of a noun ends in -a, and so does this one. That is the whole requirement, and മെലിഞ്ഞ (meliñña) meets it."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What comes in front of the -a has never been fixed. വലിയ, പുതിയ, ചെറിയ and കുറിയ (kuṟiya) end -ിയ, but നല്ല ends -ല്ല and പഴയ ends in a plain -യ. മെലിഞ്ഞ (meliñña) adds a doubled ഞ്ഞ to that list — a shape you have had since പച്ച and മഞ്ഞ, back among the colours."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "That changes nothing about how it is used — it still stands before the noun and still does not change:"
            },
            {
              "kind": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                ""
              ],
              "columns": 2,
              "rowCount": 2,
              "utterances": [
                "കുറിയ കുട്ടി, kuṟiya kuṭṭi.",
                "മെലിഞ്ഞ കുട്ടി, meliñña kuṭṭi."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "meliñña",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *meliñña*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "meliñña kuṭṭi",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *meliñña kuṭṭi*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "kuṟiya kuṭṭi, then meliñña kuṭṭi",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *kuṟiya kuṭṭi*, then *meliñña kuṭṭi*]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What is thin? (മെലിഞ്ഞ (meliñña).) What do all the adjectives so far end in? (-a.) Does this one behave any differently? (No — in front, unchanged.)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ML-C101-thadicha",
      "sequence": 3640,
      "title": "തടിച്ച (taṭicca) — stout",
      "headword": "തടിച്ച",
      "romanization": "taṭicca",
      "gloss": "stout — the far end of മെലിഞ്ഞ, on another shape that still closes on -a",
      "script": "malayalam",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:ffac7cb748afcbe6",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Say a thin child."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "തടിച്ച — taṭicca — stout, heavily built."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "തടിച്ച കുട്ടി — taṭicca kuṭṭi — \"a stout child.\""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "This is the far end of the last word, and the book has done that before: one quality, then its opposite, so a single axis costs you two words and not four."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Three shapes, one ending, one behaviour:"
            },
            {
              "kind": "table",
              "headers": [
                "adjective",
                "ends"
              ],
              "columns": 2,
              "rowCount": 3,
              "utterances": [
                "adjective: കുറിയ (kuṟiya). ends: -ിയ.",
                "adjective: മെലിഞ്ഞ (meliñña). ends: -ഞ്ഞ.",
                "adjective: തടിച്ച (taṭicca). ends: -ച്ച."
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Every one of them closes on -a, stands in front of the noun, and does not change. The shape in front of the -a varies and never matters — as നല്ല and പഴയ were already showing you before this chapter began."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "taṭicca",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *taṭicca*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "meliñña kuṭṭi, then taṭicca kuṭṭi",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *meliñña kuṭṭi*, then *taṭicca kuṭṭi*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "all three adjectives from this chapter in a row",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: all three adjectives from this chapter in a row]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What is stout? (തടിച്ച (taṭicca).) And its opposite? (മെലിഞ്ഞ (meliñña).) What do the three shapes of this chapter have in common? (They all end in -a and none of them changes.)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ML-C101-uyaram",
      "sequence": 3650,
      "title": "ഉയരം (uyaraṁ) — height",
      "headword": "ഉയരം",
      "romanization": "uyaraṁ",
      "gloss": "height — the noun that lets you say someone is tall without an adjective for it",
      "script": "malayalam",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:52455dc627c645f1",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Say short, of a person. Then say the word for there is."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ഉയരം — uyaraṁ — height."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "എനിക്ക് ഉയരമുണ്ട്. — enikkŭ uyaramuṇṭŭ — \"To me, height exists\" — I am tall."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "There is no single word for tall in this book, and this is how you say it anyway."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "കുറിയ (kuṟiya) was an adjective, so it went in front of a noun. ഉയരം (uyaraṁ) is not an adjective — it is a noun, height — so it takes the other machine you already own: the one where a thing exists to someone."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "എനിക്ക് ഉയരമുണ്ട്. — enikkŭ uyaramuṇṭŭ — to-me height there-is — I am tall."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "That frame is not new. The chapter that gave you ഉണ്ട് used it to say that someone has a thing, and the chapter on എനിക്ക് gave you the person the having happens to. All this chapter does is put a new noun into it."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "And the ം does here what it does before ആണ് — it takes the full letter മ so it can carry what follows: ഉയരം (uyaraṁ) + ഉണ്ട് becomes ഉയരമുണ്ട്."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Do not read that as a rule about every ending. The chapter on easy and hard told you the ം does different things for different endings, and this chapter's own title proves it: ഉയരം (uyaraṁ) + ഉം is ഉയരവും, with a വ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "uyaraṁ",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *uyaraṁ*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "enikkŭ uyaramuṇṭŭ",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *enikkŭ uyaramuṇṭŭ*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "why this one needs ഉണ്ട് and കുറിയ (kuṟiya) did not",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: why this one needs **ഉണ്ട്** and **കുറിയ** did not]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What is height? (ഉയരം (uyaraṁ).) How do you say I am tall? (എനിക്ക് ഉയരമുണ്ട്.) And why not an adjective, as with കുറിയ (kuṟiya)? (Because ഉയരം (uyaraṁ) is a noun — it exists to someone.)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ML-R101-build-recall",
      "sequence": 3660,
      "title": "(short, thin, stout, and height) (uyaravuṁ kuṟiyayuṁ enna ōrmma) — from cold",
      "headword": "(short, thin, stout, and height)",
      "romanization": "uyaravuṁ kuṟiyayuṁ enna ōrmma",
      "gloss": "cold retrieval of three adjectives and one noun, and of why the noun needs a different machine",
      "script": "malayalam",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:bd832df16a67c233",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Close the lessons before this one. Say short, thin, stout, and height."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "grammar",
          "title": "Grammar Lens: three of them go in front, and one cannot",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Three of this chapter's four words are adjectives, and all three behave the way every adjective in the book has:"
            },
            {
              "kind": "table",
              "headers": [
                "adjective",
                "before the noun"
              ],
              "columns": 2,
              "rowCount": 3,
              "utterances": [
                "adjective: കുറിയ. before the noun: കുറിയ കുട്ടി (kuṟiya kuṭṭi).",
                "adjective: മെലിഞ്ഞ. before the noun: മെലിഞ്ഞ കുട്ടി (meliñña kuṭṭi).",
                "adjective: തടിച്ച. before the noun: തടിച്ച കുട്ടി (taṭicca kuṭṭi)."
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "They end -ിയ, -ഞ്ഞ and -ച്ച — three different shapes, all closing on -a, none of them changing for the noun behind it."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ഉയരം (uyaraṁ) is the odd one, and not because it is irregular. It is a noun, so there is nothing for it to stand in front of. It uses the frame you were given for having:"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "എനിക്ക് ഉയരമുണ്ട്. — enikkŭ uyaramuṇṭŭ — to-me height there-is — I am tall."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The book still has no single word for tall. It has a noun for height and a way to say that someone has it, and between them that is the whole meaning."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "That is worth noticing rather than papering over: ചെറിയ and കുറിയ (kuṟiya) are almost the same word and do not mean the same thing — one is small, the other short — and tall is the mirror of neither. You reach it by another route."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "kuṟiya, meliñña, taṭicca, uyaraṁ",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *kuṟiya*, *meliñña*, *taṭicca*, *uyaraṁ*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "taṭicca kuṭṭi, then meliñña kuṭṭi",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *taṭicca kuṭṭi*, then *meliñña kuṭṭi*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "enikkŭ uyaramuṇṭŭ",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *enikkŭ uyaramuṇṭŭ*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
